{
    "__comment__": "Hardware-free setup for the Expert scan panel on STEP BOARDS (docs/devices/scan_engines.rst): two simulated boards that speak the step-engine protocol IMSWITCH_STEP/1, as a TriggerScope with its protocol firmware will (docs/devices/step-engine-protocol.rst). 'triggerscope' leads -- the Expert panel runs on it (scan.engine) -- and drives the piezo Z on dac0, the 405 and 488 lasers and the camera trigger; 'aux' follows it step by step (its triggerInput is wired to triggerscope/ttl15) and switches the 561 laser. A program on the leader's devices alone runs on the leader; one that also uses the 561 runs on both, the follower stepped by the leader's pulses. Z and the lasers are set by hand through the boards (StepBoardPositionerManager, StepBoardLaserManager). Each board declares a 1 us grid and a 20 ppm clock: the drift between two pulses must stay under half a tick, so steps of up to 12.5 ms. To use real boards, replace port \"simulated\" and simulatedBoard with the serial port, baudrate and replyTimeoutS. The NI-DAQ is simulated (every setup has its engine); no device is on it.",
    "detectors": {
        "Camera": {
            "analogChannel": null,
            "digitalLine": "triggerscope/ttl2",
            "managerName": "HamamatsuManager",
            "managerProperties": {
                "cameraListIndex": "mock",
                "hamamatsu": {
                    "trigger_source": 2,
                    "subarray_hpos": 0,
                    "subarray_vpos": 0,
                    "subarray_hsize": 512,
                    "subarray_vsize": 512,
                    "image_width": 512,
                    "image_height": 512
                }
            },
            "forAcquisition": true,
            "forFocusLock": false
        }
    },
    "lasers": {
